{"step_index":6090,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T00:58:33Z","thinking":"The failed process (PROC-013) prevented the fix from being applied before the user's action. Any past views of PROC-012, whether from history or the Excel file, were from the prior day and would not have shown the fix. Now examining the application's main file (`app.py`) and associated HTML template (`index.html`) to determine why a new tab was not visible to the user.\n\n\nThe application's entry point, `app.py`, directly loads the `index.html` template, confirming the front-end structure. This suggests a potential area to investigate for the missing tab. The user may have interacted with the application prior to the fix.\n\n\nConsidering the PowerShell history, the user was likely running the application entry point, which initiates the server. This points towards an interaction with the settings screen within the desktop application's GUI, and not a direct launch of the backend servers. Focusing on the HTML template (`index.html`), the `settings` screen contains server configuration, potentially explaining the expected server switcher.\n\n\nThe `screen-settings` still presents the outdated MSEMAX configuration, indicating a need for a unified server management approach. Integrating a server switcher directly into `screen-settings` or linking to a dedicated `screen-servers` could improve usability. The sidebar footer should be enhanced to show the active server's name and status with toggle and management buttons, and the top bar also requires the server badge.\n\n\nEnhancements to the top bar server badge are proposed: making it clickable to navigate to the server management screen and displaying the active server's name. A quick server switch card is to be integrated into the settings screen, along with a button to open the full server manager.\n\nA prominent banner showing the active server provider and port will be added to the home screen. This should immediately inform users of the current server configuration and provide a clear pathway to change it. A test implementation on the home screen is being planned.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/desktop_app/templates/index.html","EndLine":1115,"StartLine":1075,"toolAction":"Viewing start of screen-new in index.html","toolSummary":"View start of screen-new"}}]}
